 "notes": "Pots & casseroles rebuilt: 6 old kinds -> 9 (added Donabe, Tagine, Fondue set). Dutch oven now kind -> archetype -> version (Le Creuset, Staub, Lodge, Chasseur, Vermicular, vintage Griswold); old Lodge models became versions, Tramontina Cultura/Utsava ranges dropped as range spam. Pressure cooker is stovetop-only (electric multicookers to appliances); 8 Hawkins SKUs collapsed into one Hawkins Classic archetype with ranges as versions; Presto/WMF/Tefal/Zavor/Magefesa kept as plain models from the America's Test Kitchen stovetop test. Stockpot cut from 4 Tramontina models and 5 ranges to one entry. Cookware set kept 13 models: market brands plus Consumer Reports and America's Test Kitchen winners (marked in model names). Left out: Safi/Fez Moroccan tagine pottery, Wagner and Nambu iron (no page retrieved this session), Kuhn Rikon fondue (no source), Presto as archetype (history not confirmed). Founding years for Fissler, Spring, Emile Henry, All-Clad, Calphalon, Made In, GreenPan, HexClad, Tefal, TTK Prestige left blank because not on retrieved pages. Sources: Wikipedia (Le Creuset, Staub, Lodge, Dutch oven, Pressure cooker, Kuhn Rikon, Fissler, Hawkins Cookers, TTK Prestige, Donabe, Iga ware, Banko ware, Tagine, Caquelon, Food steamer, Saucepan, Griswold, All-Clad, Tramontina, Cuisinart, Made In, HexClad, Tefal, WMF), maker pages (Mauviel, Ruffoni, Fissler, Hawkins, Nagatani-en/Toiro, Spring brandshop, Zwilling/Staub, Le Creuset heritage, Calphalon, GreenPan), Monocle (Vermicular), La Trésorerie (Chasseur), Williams-Sonoma (Emile Henry), Consumer Reports and America's Test Kitchen tests.",
